          "quote": "PWM/servo driver NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "PWM driver responds at 0x41 instead of 0x40, so firmware expecting 0x40 will not control servos.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["U5"],
      "pins": ["U5.7"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V"],
      "observed": "BMI088 protocol select pin PS (pin 7) is connected to +3.3V.",
      "expected": "PS should be tied to GND to select I2C mode, as the design uses I2C addresses 0x19/0x69.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"PS\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "IMU (accel + gyro) Bosch BMI088, I2C addr 0x19 (acc) / 0x69 (gyr)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "IMU enters SPI mode and does not respond to I2C, so navigation computer cannot read inertial data.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U7"],
      "pins": ["U7.1"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U7-SS-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "MPRLS0025PA00001A slave-select pin SS (pin 1) is left unconnected.",
      "expected": "In I2C mode, SS must be tied to VDD (3.3V) to enable the I2C interface.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"303\") (name \"unconnected-(U7-SS-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"SS\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Absolute pressure sensor (barometer) Honeywell MPRLS0025PA00001A, I2C addr 0x18"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Barometer does not respond to I2C, so altitude/pressure data is unavailable.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain several pin-level deviations from the specification. The most confident are the PCA9685 address pin A0 tied high (changing its I2C address to 0x41), the BMI088 PS pin tied high (selecting SPI instead of I2C), and the MPRLS SS pin left floating (disabling its I2C interface)."
}

